  "body": "Closes #4254\n\nCoverage breach issues can now recover across different Gate producer runs. Restore the repository's accumulated history before evaluation, replace repeated producer-run records, retain at most 30 samples, and save an immutable guard-run cache afterward. Incomplete recovery reports how many records meet the existing threshold. Baselines, warning allowances and recovery-window defaults are preserved.\n\nThe consumer workflow receives the same history lifecycle while retaining its existing token, download and action-pin differences. The sync manifest and integration guide describe the shared contract.\n\nValidation:\n- `/opt/anaconda3/bin/python3 -m pytest tests/test_coverage_guard.py tests/test_coverage_guard_payload_location.py tests/test_coverage_guard_payload_matching.py tests/workflows/test_maint_coverage_guard_artifacts.py -q --no-cov`: 135 passed.\n- Deliberate break: disconnecting accumulation made `test_recovery_window_counts_records_accumulated_across_runs` fail because the third recovered sample could not close the issue. Exact-byte restoration returned the focused suite to green.\n- Black, Ruff, actionlint for both workflows, and `git diff --check` pass.\n\nHosted cache continuity, current-head CI and the seven-minute review floor remain pending. This PR does not claim a deployed recovery or close an existing baseline-breach issue.\n\n<!-- pr-preamble:start -->\n<!-- meta:issue:4254 -->\n> **Source:** Issue #4254\n\nCloses #4254\n\n<!-- pr-preamble:end -->\n\n<!-- auto-status-summary:start -->\n## Automated Status Summary\n#### Scope\n_Scope section missing from source issue._\n\n<!-- Updated WORKFLOW_OUTPUTS.md context:start -->\n## Context for Agent\n\n### Related Issues/PRs\n- [#4011](https://github.com/stranske/Workflows/issues/4011)\n- [#2933](https://github.com/stranske/Workflows/issues/2933)\n- [#180](https://github.com/stranske/Workflows/issues/180)\n<!-- Updated WORKFLOW_OUTPUTS.md context:end -->\n\n#### Tasks\n- [x] `.github/workflows/maint-coverage-guard.yml:425`: make the history cache key repository-scoped instead of producer-run-scoped, with a restore prefix, so the previous guard run's accumulated history is restored before the check.\n- [x] `tools/coverage_guard.py:593` (`_recovery_window_satisfied`) and its caller near `:763`: before the check, append the current trend record to the restored history (replacing a record with the same run id), keep at most 30 records, and write the file back so the cache saves it.\n- [x] `tools/coverage_guard.py:763`: say in the message how many records the window holds and how many it needs, for example \"recovered, 2 of 3 records at or above the baseline\".\n\n#### Acceptance criteria\n- [x] Named test: `tests/test_coverage_guard.py::test_recovery_window_counts_records_accumulated_across_runs`: a restored history of two records at or above the baseline plus the current record satisfies a 3-record window; the current record alone does not; the same run id is not counted twice.\n- [x] Deliberate-break \u2192 revert: remove the append of the current record to the restored history, confirm the named test FAILS, then revert.\n- [x] Named test: `tests/test_coverage_guard.py::test_recovery_message_names_records_held_and_needed` asserts the \"N of M records\" text.\n\n<!-- auto-status-summary:end -->",
